  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets of the sleeping night.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold, devoid of cheer.\n\nLike ghosts they passed, a spectral crowd,\nWith faces lost, unseeing, loud\nIn worlds of their own, deep and wide,\nWith nowhere left for him to hide.\n\nAmidst the sea of urban stone,\nHe stood alone, entirely alone.\nA profound solitude, deep and vast,\nWatching the city shadows cast.\n\n***\n\nGiraffe"
